17:05:16,427 root DEBUG {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You will be given a SQL query and some strategies to rewrite the given SQL query. Your task is to cluster the provided query rewrite strategies.\n\nOutput a python list of objects encapsulated with ```python and ```, where each object is a python list of strategy indexes corresponding to a cluster.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '\nSQL Query:\n```sql\nSELECT MIN(chn.name) AS character,\n       MIN(t.title) AS movie_with_american_producer\nFROM char_name AS chn,\n     cast_info AS ci,\n     company_name AS cn,\n     company_type AS ct,\n     movie_companies AS mc,\n     role_type AS rt,\n     title AS t\nWHERE ci.note LIKE \'%(producer)%\'\n  AND cn.country_code = \'[us]\'\n  AND t.production_year > 1990\n  AND t.id = mc.movie_id\n  AND t.id = ci.movie_id\n  AND ci.movie_id = mc.movie_id\n  AND chn.id = ci.person_role_id\n  AND rt.id = ci.role_id\n  AND cn.id = mc.company_id\n  AND ct.id = mc.company_type_id;\n```\n\nQuery Rewrite Strategies:\nQuery Rewrite 1:\n"""The given SQL query does not contain any repeated function calls or operations that can be moved outside of loops. However, we can apply some transformations to optimize the query:\n\n* Since the aggregate functions are deterministic and not dependent on row-specific data, we can replace them with pre-calculated columns.\n* The `LIKE` operation is used in a constant pattern, which does not change frequently. We can create a temporary table or CTE that calculates the result of this function once and then join it with the main query.\n\nHere\'s an example of how the rewritten query could look:\n```sql\nWITH PreCalculated AS (\n  SELECT chn.name as character,\n         t.title as movie_with_american_producer,\n         CASE WHEN ci.note LIKE \'%(producer)%\' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END as producer_flag\n  FROM char_name AS chn,\n       cast_info AS ci,\n       company_name AS cn,\n       company_type AS ct,\n       movie_companies AS mc,\n       role_type AS rt,\n       title AS t\n)\nSELECT MIN(character) as character,\n       MIN(movie_with_american_producer) as movie_with_american_producer\nFROM PreCalculated\nWHERE producer_flag = 1;\n```\nNote that this is just an example, and the actual rewritten query may vary depending on the specific requirements and constraints of the original query."""'}], 'response': 'Here are the clusters for the provided SQL query rewrite strategies:\n\n```python\n[\n    [0],  # The given SQL query does not contain any repeated function calls or operations that can be moved outside of loops.\n    [1]   # Since the aggregate functions are deterministic and not dependent on row-specific data, we can replace them with pre-calculated columns.\n]\n```\n\nNote: There is only one strategy provided for rewriting the SQL query.', 'time': 0.913954496383667}
